    "goal": "Make tests/test_harness_home_carries_the_operator_config.py state the fence its cases depend on, since five of them fail on main with KeyError CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR. The harness-home carry was written while workers launched fenced by default, and it merged after 39fd7a28 made workers launch unfenced (FENCE_WORKERS = False in reckon/crew/dispatch.py) and made a run adopt its own harness home only when fenced. So an unfenced launch sets no CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, and cases that expect a run home now fail. Cases exercising the carry must opt into the fence explicitly (fence=True on launch_plan, or FENCE_WORKERS monkeypatched to True), as fence-tests-opt-into-the-fence did for the fenced-resume tests. A case that asserts unfenced behaviour must assert that the operator home is kept. The failing ids are test_a_claude_run_home_carries_the_operator_settings_and_instructions, test_a_lane_that_declares_a_missing_file_seeds_without_it, test_a_claude_resume_places_the_operator_transcript, test_a_fresh_launch_copies_no_transcript and test_the_operator_home_is_never_read_or_written. Change no product code.",
